# The cellarer's tallies: success scene for the writing spot.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_MonTallies

== start ==
Two hundred pages of a working household: grain bought, candles bought, wool bought. Neat columns, initialed.

Then the last winter, and the purchases stop. On purpose. No candles this quarter, marked *not needed*. No salt. No lamp oil.

* [Read to the end.] -> final

== final ==
The final pages are not purchases at all. The cellarer counted everything the house had left and divided it: this much food, this many mouths, this many weeks. He wrote down the answer and initialed it.

They knew exactly when the house would die. They chose the date themselves.

The last line: we will not need the spring seed.

* [Close the ledger.] -> end
